<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Connachta</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Connachta were a group of early Irish dynasties who claimed descent from the legendary king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conn-of-the-hundred-battles">Conn of the Hundred Battles</a> and gave their name to the province of Connacht. Their main branches, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-briuin">Uí Briúin</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-fiachrach">Uí Fiachrach</a> and Uí Ailello, ruled the province, and the O'Connor kings of Connacht, who rose from the Uí Briúin, became high kings of Ireland in the 12th century.</p></div>
